First, let's calculate the time John spends driving:

1. **Driving Time:**
   - First 2 hours in standstill traffic
   - Next 2 hours driving at 30 mph
   - Last 2 hours driving at 80 mph

   Calculate each segment:
   - First 2 hours: \( 2 \text{ hours} \times 60 \text{ mph} = 120 \text{ miles} \)
   - Next 2 hours: \( 2 \text{ hours} \times 30 \text{ mph} = 60 \text{ miles} \)
   - Last 2 hours: \( 2 \text{ hours} \times 80 \text{ mph} = 160 \text{ miles} \)

   Total driving time = \( 120 \text{ miles} + 60 \text{ miles} + 160 \text{ miles} = 340 \text{ miles} \)

2. **Total Time:**
   - Total time = 3 hours (driving) + 2 hours (stalled) = 5 hours

